  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the Carmel Central School District to offer a separate\nreferendum on the question of term limits for members of the Carmel Central\nSchool District board of education",
    "basePrintNo": "S6093",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6093-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6093\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act authorizing the Carmel Central School District to offer a sepa-\nrate referendum on the question of term limits for members of the Carmel\nCentral School District board of education\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAuthorizes the Carmel Central School District to offer a separate refer-\nendum on the question of term limits for members of the Carmel Central\nSchool District board of education\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes Carmel Central School district in the town of\nPatterson, Putnam County, to offer voters a separate referendum regard-\ning the question of term limits for members who serve on the school\nboard on the same day as the annual school budget vote.\n\nSection 2 states the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnder current law, individual school boards are unable to establish term\nlimits for Board of Education members, either by board decision or\npublic referendum. There is much debate over the question of term\nlimits- some believe they are a healthy way to promote the democratic\nprocess, while others argue that they will unnecessarily prevent experi-\nenced and qualified candidates from remaining in office.\n\nThe individuals living within Carmel Central School district should be\ngiven the opportunity to decide for themselves whether they would like\nto implement such term limits for those who represent both the community\nand our young ones. This legislation comes at the request of the Carmel\nCentral School District Board of Education.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
